2.0 Team Allocation
Competitors are free to form their own teams consisting of EXACTLY 4 people in one team. In order to make your own teams, ONLY ONE person from the team fills out this form with all the necessary details Please note that upon the discretion of the YEC Chair and YEC Vice Chairs, team members are subject to change.  Feel free to be creative with your group names, please make sure to NOT have a controversial group name. Doing so will result in the name being nullified and a number being assigned instead 


3.0 Competition Description and Objective
The goal of the Junior Design competition is to challenge Junior Engineering Students to design and build a prototype to address a technical problem. Teams in Junior Team Design are required to brainstorm and design their project during the limited time provided in the first half of the competition and then present an oral presentation with an accompanying digital presentation to demonstrate their design in the second half of the competition. The oral presentation should summarize the design process, the design itself, and any unique aspects of the design.
3.1 Team Composition and Eligibility
Team Size: Must consist of exactly 4 members
Eligibility: All Competitors must be enrolled in a York Undergraduate Program. All competitors and teams must also meet the requirements outlined by the Lassonde Engineering Society. The team must be entirely composed of students who, at the time of registration, have not yet completed 50% or more of the minimum number of credits required to complete their respective accredited engineering programs.
