4.0 Competition Details
4.1 Resources
On the day of the competition, teams will be provided with all the materials needed to build a prototype that solves a given problem. While there is no spending cap, each item has a set price and a limited available quantity. Teams must track the cost of the materials they use to calculate their final prototype budget
4.2 Competitor Deliverables
Submission:
Your team must submit the following at the time mentioned in Phase 2. 


1. Physical prototype of the design
2. Budget of the whole project
3. Presentation Document in PPT or PDF file:
   1. If the use of any external resources are present, then references must be included and in IEEE citation format.
   2. File name: 
      1. [Team Name] - Junior_Design_Presentation.pdf or 
      2. [Team Name] - Junior_Design_Presentation.pptx
   3. Submit your slideshow to this form.
If you are having issues, email the submissions to yec@lasengsoc.com. The subject line of the email should be: [Team Name] - Junior Design Presentation
A final budget and cost of each team's solutions must be included within their presentation.  


Some things you may want to incorporate into your presentation includes, but are not limited to:
1. Pictures of the design schematics and process
2. Description of the building and testing process
3. Pictures of the finished product
4. Justification (Why did you use that material)


You may not edit your presentation after submitting it. You only have the time given to you for working on the solution and its presentation.
