7.0 Evaluation
7.1 Judging
Judging will be based on the ability of the structure to protect the egg, as well as the quality of the team’s presentation. The order of presentations will be shared near the end of Phase 1 of the competition.


Each team will present their structure to the judges. Following these presentations, the structures will then be tested using their launching mechanisms from a constant height of 29 inches toward the target field 80 inches away. Then, the next group of nine teams will present and test their structures, and so on, until every group has presented.
One last round will take place, where the top three best structures will be put up against each other, where the winner will be determined.
